The post-merge re-scan of the 2026-10-05 audit (#1479, #1481) left 10
files flagged: 3 already verified as true negatives, and these 7
extended1 analyzers, all [days]-only and all floored by the Phase-3
TreeSitterAnalyzer migration (cfd3132756). Two read-only reviewers read
them in full; all 7 had real drift and 4 had reproduced code bugs.

- verilog: instantiations are edges, not symbols; enclosing module by
  position; case-insensitive, module-preferring lookup and its 0.90 /
  0.50 / 0.70 confidences.
- zig: kinds include methods, fields, variables; comptime has no special
  handling (B); call path hints, deferral, placeholder. Known gaps
  stated: enclosing function by name (INV-musij), @import emitted twice
  (INV-vasak).
- kdl, bibtex: "single-pass orchestration" was wrong (B: the base class
  always runs two passes; these extract no edges); kdl sections are any
  node with children, at any depth (B); bibtex kind is always entry,
  journal is not captured, no citation edges.
- llvm_ir: calls to undefined functions are dropped; Pass 2 re-walks
  the file. Known gaps: caller by name (INV-nafij), indirect call
  credited to an argument (INV-nupak).
- wolfram: calls come from the file node, deduplicated per callee; only
  Get/Needs/Import calls are imports (not <<package`). Known gaps:
  definitions counted as calls, .m files never analyzed (INV-kafir).
- cobol: data items from every DATA DIVISION section; 0.85 confidence
  scaling and unresolved edges for both PERFORM and CALL. Known gaps:
  PERFORM repo-wide, section headers do not update the caller
  (INV-lutaj). Separately, the noise filter drops section/paragraph in
  every language, hiding all COBOL call edges (INV-sizap).

The by-name enclosing-callable defect is now in three analyzers plus
agda (code-read): filed as a family with a proposed gate (WI-kosar).
AST with docstrings stripped: all 7 files identical.

